+  RIPPS2 build 100 (user: "make it so we aren't sharing settings with other opl elf and ours is separate clean and
+  structured without any bloat so the save will be small neat and display the icn"): with a memory card in, RIPPS2's
+  settings are a save of their own, mcN:/RIPPS2: the hat (icon.sys, ripps2.icn) and the settings files, nothing else.
+  Not beside the ELF, where another OPL's conf files sit, nor in OPL's mc?:OPL. The boot card first, then the other.
+  haveSettings: only a card whose RIPPS2 folder holds RIPPS2's settings already (the load); otherwise the first card
+  in, its folder made with its hat (the save). A Custom Settings Path (config.path) wins over both; without a card
